1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,198
This is AI4S Chip Photo Review, a research tool for microscope photos of
organ-on-a-chip samples.

2
00:00:06,198 --> 00:00:09,771
It places likely poor-quality samples earlier in a review list.

3
00:00:09,771 --> 00:00:11,335
A person makes the decision.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,090
The tool first checks the image format.

5
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:24,504
Small or unfamiliar formats go to manual review without an automatic score.

6
00:00:24,504 --> 00:00:29,307
Accepted images become gray images with a long side of 1,036 pixels.

7
00:00:29,307 --> 00:00:33,535
Frozen DINOv2 features combine a whole-photo view with nine tiles.

8
00:00:33,535 --> 00:00:36,213
A small trained model produces the review score.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,286
This is the command that runs the photo tool.

10
00:00:44,286 --> 00:00:49,963
The table contains actual saved output from a verified fresh Kaggle
installation on October eighth.

11
00:00:49,963 --> 00:00:52,227
Twelve photos received scores and ranks.

12
00:00:52,227 --> 00:00:56,907
Five photos went to manual review, including small and unfamiliar formats.

13
00:00:56,907 --> 00:01:01,619
The output includes the filename, format, route, score, and rank.

14
00:01:01,619 --> 00:01:05,333
This CPU demonstration took 402.8 seconds.

15
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,135
The top row shows the first four photos in the review list.

16
00:01:21,135 --> 00:01:22,924
The bottom row shows the last four.

17
00:01:22,924 --> 00:01:25,592
This small demonstration illustrates operation.

18
00:01:25,592 --> 00:01:27,331
It is not an accuracy estimate.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,666
The primary result uses 672 reserved photos scored automatically by both
methods.

20
00:01:45,666 --> 00:01:53,538
The ranking score, called AUC, was 0.850 with tiles and 0.810 with the whole
photo alone.

21
00:01:53,538 --> 00:02:02,014
The paired increase was 0.040, with a 95 percent range from 0.015 to 0.067.

22
00:02:02,014 --> 00:02:06,956
AUC measures ranking quality. It does not mean 85 percent accuracy.

23
00:02:06,956 --> 00:02:09,808
Review curves do not measure human time savings.

24
00:02:10,625 --> 00:02:14,888
Scores decreased when related filename groups were also excluded from
training.

25
00:02:14,888 --> 00:02:18,362
We withdrew the earlier claim of no loss on unseen cell types.

26
00:02:18,362 --> 00:02:21,578
The tile method still ranked better in the corrected comparison.

27
00:02:21,578 --> 00:02:25,493
Small photos remained a weakness, so they go to manual review.

28
00:02:25,493 --> 00:02:29,901
Extra training and heat-map explanations did not justify stronger claims.

29
00:02:34,625 --> 00:02:37,693
Separate nucleus studies used fifty reserved images.

30
00:02:37,693 --> 00:02:43,491
B02 reduced average count error from 4.93 to 4.31 nuclei per image.

31
00:02:43,491 --> 00:02:50,732
At different settings, B03 increased the strict outline score from 0.855 to
0.901.

32
00:02:50,732 --> 00:02:55,642
The images share plates with development images, so this is not a new-
laboratory test.

33
00:02:56,458 --> 00:02:58,957
Strong artificial noise caused large errors.

34
00:02:58,957 --> 00:03:03,067
Training with noise helped under that noise type, but made clean counting
worse.

35
00:03:03,067 --> 00:03:08,412
Only about forty-three percent of the smallest tenth of nuclei were found at
the looser overlap level.

36
00:03:08,412 --> 00:03:13,190
Outside color images had strict outline scores below 0.001.

37
00:03:13,190 --> 00:03:15,188
The models also shared mistakes.

38
00:03:18,458 --> 00:03:21,990
We also compared controllers in a repaired droplet simulator.

39
00:03:21,990 --> 00:03:32,364
On harder conditions, learned control had mean size error of 1.333
micrometers, versus 1.946 and 2.062 for two rule controllers.

40
00:03:32,364 --> 00:03:38,206
One learned-control episode still spent 25.3 percent of steps outside the
operating range.

41
00:03:38,206 --> 00:03:40,047
No physical chip was operated.

42
00:03:40,875 --> 00:03:45,574
A fresh Kaggle setup reproduced the photo pipeline and one nucleus training
split.

43
00:03:45,574 --> 00:03:48,276
It did not rebuild every model or supporting study.

44
00:03:48,276 --> 00:03:52,061
The rebuilt scorer completed the ordinary fresh-install demonstration.

45
00:03:52,061 --> 00:03:56,019
The additional strict cloud test failed with no useful diagnostic log.

46
00:03:56,019 --> 00:03:57,863
That failure remains in the report.

47
00:04:02,875 --> 00:04:06,277
The measured benefit is better review order on the stated dataset.

48
00:04:06,277 --> 00:04:12,165
Human time savings, transfer to another chip laboratory, and physical
control remain unproven.

49
00:04:12,165 --> 00:04:16,717
The next steps are independently labeled chip data and a timed study with
researchers.

50
00:04:16,717 --> 00:04:19,674
A person stays responsible for sample decisions.

51
00:04:22,875 --> 00:04:26,358
The write-up contains the full experiment record and source credits.

52
00:04:26,358 --> 00:04:30,167
The full write-up contains the reproduction instructions and resource links.

53
00:04:30,167 --> 00:04:33,094
Thank you for reviewing AI4S Chip Photo Review.
